    "done_when": "tests/test_reservation_is_shared_across_projects.py passes under the root .venv python, in a temporary RECKON_HOME, with four cases. (1) Placement resolution under project B returns the job id that a dispatch under project A published, because one unkeyed host-global record replaces the per-project keying in reckon/crew/placement.py. (2) The reservation roster refusal in reckon/crew/dispatch.py (_refuse_over_reservation_roster) counts only runs whose live pointer records placement into that reservation, across every project. This is asserted over one backend's population holding placed and unplaced runs from two projects: the unplaced runs are not counted, and the placed runs of both projects are. (3) A backend declaring no placement is untouched and unbounded by the roster. (4) Migration: with no host-global record present and only a legacy per-project record on disk (the shape of today's placement/imas-ambix/reservation.json), a dispatch under that project declaring placement still resolves that record's job id. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Existing tests in tests/test_crew_placement_reservation.py and tests/test_placement_steps_under_reservation.py that pin per-project keying are updated, with the before and after assertion stated in the manifest. Those two files, the new test and the other files importing reckon.crew.placement show 0 added failures between a base arm and a head arm. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and command and ending EXIT=. Out of scope, listed as follow_ons: holding a reservation when no record is published, the two-dispatch one-allocation assertion, and adopting 1277272. No real scheduler command runs; nothing touches the operator's real placement records.",
